# the SMK-37 Elite's pads and faders (ui.c pads_input): a pad holds one of PERFORM's sixteen white-key effects on any
# page; > latches; < lets everything go; a knob turned with a pad down throws a master action, which goes back when
# the pads are up; the faders are the mix, or (FADER BANK) the master actions, and do nothing until moved
wait 300
expect view 0
expect pnow 0
# pad 0: Stutter (key 0); pad 5: Macalla (key 9), together; on the home page, not PERFORM
pad 0 down
expect padfx 1
expect pnow 1
pad 5 down
expect padfx 513
expect pnow 513
pad 0 up
expect pnow 512
pad 5 up
expect pnow 0
expect view 0
# the bottom row: pad 8 Reverb (key 14), pad 15 Crush (key 26)
pad 8 down
expect pnow 16384
pad 8 up
pad 15 down
expect pnow 67108864
pad 15 up
expect pnow 0
# on a layer's page too
tap CHORD
wait 300
expect view 1
tappad 2
expect pnow 0
pad 2 down
expect pnow 16
pad 2 up
tap PATCH
wait 300
expect view 0
# > held and a pad hit: latched, > lit; the pad up, it stays; hit again with >: let go
press >
pad 10 down
expect padlatch 262144
pad 10 up
release >
wait 100
expect pnow 262144
expect xlit 8
pad 1 down
expect pnow 262148
pad 1 up
expect pnow 262144
press >
tappad 10
release >
expect padlatch 0
expect pnow 0
expect xlit 0
# < : every latch let go, the pads told to rest
press >
tappad 3
tappad 4
release >
expect padlatch 192
tap <
expect padlatch 0
expect pnow 0
expect padrests 1
# a throw: a pad down, KNOB 1 (K5) turned: Filter moves; the pad up: back at 0. The page's own knob did not move
mark
expect mac0 0
pad 0 down
turn K5 8
expect mac0 6
turn K7 -5
expect mac2 -3
pad 0 up
wait 50
expect mac0 0
expect mac2 0
expect marked 0
# no pad down: KNOB 1 is the page's own again (HOME's Filter: it stays where it is put)
turn K5 8
expect mac0 6
turn K5 -6
expect mac0 0
# the faders: nothing until moved (the first position seen is where it is)
mark
fader 0 500
fader 1 500
fader 2 500
fader 3 500
wait 100
expect marked 0
fader 0 1023
expect level0 100
fader 0 0
expect level0 0
listen
fader 3 519
expect level2 51
wait 50
said LEAD
fader 3 521
expect level2 51
# FADER BANK: the master actions, lit; a fader takes its new job when next moved; the middle is 0
tap FADER_BANK
expect fbank 1
expect xlit 2
expect mac0 0
expect level0 0
fader 0 1023
expect mac0 50
expect level0 0
fader 0 0
expect mac0 -50
fader 0 511
expect mac0 0
fader 1 1023
expect mac1 50
fader 1 511
expect mac1 0
tap FADER_BANK
expect fbank 0
expect xlit 0
